    "goal": "Co-incubate CYP3A4 with testosterone in the presence of a competitive inhibitor and report the run-condition IC50 and inhibitor:substrate molar ratio.",
    "rationale": "CYP3A4-mediated testosterone hydroxylation is inhibited competitively. The run-condition IC50 follows Cheng–Prusoff: IC50 = Ki(1 + [S]/Km) = 217.9 × (1 + 2721.6/1181.0) ≈ 720 µM. The inhibitor:substrate molar ratio is [I]/[S] = 233.3/2721.6 ≈ 0.086. Substrate is present well above Km ([S]/Km ≈ 2.3), so the run-condition IC50 is ~3.3× the intrinsic Ki.",
